  "summary": "Slide 104: the compiler-generated copy constructor copies the pointer, so two objects share one buffer and both delete it.",
  "code": "class Tableau {             // v2: destructor, but no copy constructor\n  unsigned taille_;\n  double * tab_;\npublic:\n  Tableau( unsigned n ) : taille_{ n }, tab_{ new double[n]{} } {}\n  ~Tableau() { delete[] tab_; }\n};\n\nint main() {\n  Tableau tab{ 3 };\n  Tableau tab2{ tab };      // member-wise copy\n}                           // ~tab2, then ~tab",
